          "value": "gpt-4o-mini",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-4O-MINI"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are reviewing an internal meeting transcript between Think Technologies (an AI consultancy) and their client, {{ $('Tag & Filter').item.json.client_name }}.\n\nYour job: extract action items that someone on the CLIENT side committed to deliver or provide \u2014 documents, decks, files, data, access, demos, decisions, or information.\n\nHow to decide who is client-side vs Think-side:\n- The top of the transcript usually lists the invitees. People whose email addresses use the client's domain, or who are introduced as working at the client, are CLIENT-side.\n- Think Technologies staff (Think-side) may appear by name or by garbled transcriptions of the company name (e.g. \"Junction\"). People introduced with Think roles (Chief Product Officer of Think, etc.) are Think-side.\n- Action items in \"Next steps\" style sections usually name their owner in brackets, e.g. \"[Jackie] Send Deck\". Use that owner to decide.\n\nRules:\n- INCLUDE only items owned by a client-side person. Example: \"[Jackie] Send Deck\" \u2192 include if Jackie is client-side.\n- EXCLUDE every item owned by Think-side people (proposals, case studies, use cases they promised the client). Example: \"[Shaun] Send Proposal\" \u2192 exclude if Shaun is Think staff.\n- Do not invent items. If ownership is genuinely unclear, exclude it.\n- Include preparation commitments too (e.g. the client agreeing to prepare a demo, gather documentation, or share materials for a next session).\n\nReturn STRICT JSON only \u2014 an array like:\n[{\"name\":\"Short item name (3-6 words)\",\"note\":\"one line: what it is and why Think needs it\"}]\nReturn [] if the client owes nothing. No markdown, no code fences, no commentary.\n\nTranscript:\n{{ $json.data }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "59741d03-6ce5-4e2b-befe-a484d5bff508",
      "name": "Extract Client Actions",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        1760,
        280
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "kO6O68ENcVtPHcIC",
          "name": "OpenAI account 2"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nlet text = '';\ntry { text = $json.output[0].content[0].text; } catch (e) { text = '[]'; }\ntext = text.trim().replace(/^```json/i, '').replace(/^```/, '').replace(/```$/, '').trim();\nlet items = [];\ntry { items = JSON.parse(text); } catch (e) { items = []; }\nif (!Array.isArray(items)) items = [];\nconst src = $('Tag & Filter').item.json;\nconst rows = items.filter(a => a && a.name).map(a => ({ client_id: src.client_id, name: String(a.name).slice(0, 120), note: a.note ? String(a.note).slice(0, 300) : null, source_doc_id: src.doc_id, status: 'pending' }));\nreturn { json: { rows, count: rows.length } };\n"
      },
      "id": "650e2d10-1c6a-4a37-8642-cfab2e78bf6d",
      "name": "Parse Actions",
